# `List` — ordered, indexed, duplicates

## Core operations

```java
List<String> names = new ArrayList<>();
names.add("Ada");            // append → index 0
names.get(1);                // read by index
names.set(0, "Alan");        // replace
names.indexOf("Ada");        // first match
names.remove("Ada");         // by value (first match)
names.remove(0);             // by index — different method!
```

**Trap:** on `List<Integer>`, `remove(2)` removes *index 2*, not the value → `remove(Integer.valueOf(2))`.

## `ArrayList` — the default

- **`get`/`set` O(1)** · append **O(1) amortised**
- Insert/remove in the **middle O(n)** (elements shift)
- Pre-size if known: `new ArrayList<>(1000)`

## `LinkedList` — rarely

`get(i)` is O(n), cache-unfriendly → **default to `ArrayList`**; for a queue/stack use `ArrayDeque`.

## Java 21 endpoints (`SequencedCollection`)

`getFirst()` · `getLast()` · `addFirst()` · `reversed()`
